WEBVTT

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.528
We are the Borg.

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:07.733
Existence as you know it
is over.

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:09.503
We will add your biological

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:12.306
and technological
distinctiveness to our own.

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.505
Resistance is...

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:12.429
The cardinal... is a thief.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:15.866
I delivered two portraits
of his mindless nephew

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:18.063
more than three months ago

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:20.698
to be depicted
in the heroic mode

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:23.208
of an Hercules or an Achilles...

00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:25.403
so specified our contract.

00:02:25.444 --> 00:02:26.877
I complied...

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:29.211
making that young fool
of a nephew

00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:32.581
look far more heroic
than nature ever intended...

00:02:32.618 --> 00:02:36.145
an act on my part far greater
than anything accomplished

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:38.953
by Hercules or Achilles.

00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:41.687
And what have I,
the divine Leonardo da Vinci,

00:02:41.727 --> 00:02:43.194
received in payment?

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:45.754
The cardinal's
eternal gratitude?

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.288
Esatto!

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:49.494
In other words, signorina...

00:02:49.535 --> 00:02:51.264
less than nothing.

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:54.603
All the more reason why you
should accept my proposal.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.870
Money is beside the point,
signo...

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:58.103
Catarina, is it?

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.338
Yes.

00:02:59.378 --> 00:03:02.506
I'm only asking for a corner,
one bench...

00:03:02.548 --> 00:03:04.448
a place to work
on my own projects...

00:03:04.483 --> 00:03:06.610
paintings, sculptures.

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:11.112
Just being here in your company
is inspiring to me.

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:14.092
Flattery, Catarina,
is also beside the point.

00:03:14.126 --> 00:03:17.584
Besides, I prefer my solitude.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:18.597
Scusami.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.125
Meraviglioso.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.967
What will you call it?

00:03:26.038 --> 00:03:28.233
"The arm of Hephaestus."

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:30.265
The god of the forge.

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:32.436
Every blacksmith
who has ever swung a hammer

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:35.106
will thank me for this creation.

00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:36.409
Someone once said...

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:38.679
"All invention is
but an extension

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:40.515
of the body of man."

00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:43.754
Do not think

00:03:43.789 --> 00:03:46.815
that just because I have
enjoyed your visit today

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:49.123
that I am prepared
to turn my workshop

00:03:49.161 --> 00:03:50.355
into a traveler's inn.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:53.993
Che cazzo!

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.159
Here... let me help you.

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:58.534
You will get your hands
covered in goose grease.

00:03:58.571 --> 00:03:59.799
It's good for the skin.

00:04:02.074 --> 00:04:05.202
Let us see if we can find
his big brother.

00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:07.712
Hopefully, he will be stronger.

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:23.788
This looks
like a flying machine.

00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:25.387
I thought that
because my imagination

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:27.922
took flight so easily
my body could do the same.

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:29.298
I was wrong.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:34.703
It's this...
flapping approach.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.731
You've designed your machine

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:39.802
to mimic the way
a bat or a sparrow flies.

00:04:39.845 --> 00:04:40.812
Yes, yes.

00:04:40.846 --> 00:04:41.904
So?

00:04:41.947 --> 00:04:43.744
So what if you based it...

00:04:45.751 --> 00:04:47.844
on the hawk instead?

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:51.182
The hawk.

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:56.488
A creature that glides
through the air.

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:58.326
Esatto.

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:05.430
We will design a new machine...

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:08.031
and, you, Catarina,
will help me fly it.

00:05:08.074 --> 00:05:09.871
I'll need someplace to work.

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:11.342
A corner?

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:12.935
One workbench?

00:05:12.978 --> 00:05:14.946
That will be fine.

00:05:15.047 --> 00:05:15.945
Ten scudi a week

00:05:16.048 --> 00:05:17.913
and you provide
your own materials.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.417
Seven...

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:22.080
and I might need to borrow
a few things on occasion.

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:23.952
Then we have an agreement.

00:05:24.056 --> 00:05:25.148
Chakotay to Janeway.

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:26.158
Go ahead.

00:05:26.192 --> 00:05:27.750
Captain, we need you
in Engineering.

00:05:27.793 --> 00:05:29.454
There's something here
you should see.

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.292
On my way.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.662
Computer, end program.

00:05:36.068 --> 00:05:36.966
What have you got?

00:05:37.069 --> 00:05:38.263
Some bad news.

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:39.862
The long-range probe
we sent out two months ago

00:05:39.905 --> 00:05:40.894
has stopped transmitting.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:41.964
At first, I thought
it was a problem

00:05:42.074 --> 00:05:43.439
with the communications grid.

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:45.205
Then I cleared up the last
few seconds of telemetry.

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:46.370
Take a look at this.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.852
This could be it, Captain.

00:05:58.224 --> 00:05:59.350
Borg space.

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:03.694
We don't know exactly
how many vessels are out there,

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:06.163
but their space
appears to be vast.

00:06:06.198 --> 00:06:08.894
It includes thousands
of solar systems...

00:06:08.934 --> 00:06:10.629
all Borg.

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:13.433
We are, no doubt, entering
the heart of their territory.

00:06:13.472 --> 00:06:15.303
There's no going around it.

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:17.969
But there may be a way
through it.

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:22.908
Before the probe was disabled,

00:06:22.948 --> 00:06:25.815
it picked up
a narrow corridor of space

00:06:25.851 --> 00:06:27.682
devoid of Borg activity.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.950
We've nicknamed it
"The Northwest Passage."

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:32.490
Unfortunately,
the passage is filled

00:06:32.525 --> 00:06:34.550
with intense
gravimetric distortions

00:06:34.593 --> 00:06:37.619
probably caused by a string
of quantum singularities.

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:39.654
Better to ride the rapids
than face the hive.

00:06:39.698 --> 00:06:41.427
Exactly. We're going
to set a course

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:44.334
for that corridor
and go into full tactical alert.

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:45.860
Where do we stand with weapons?

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:47.736
I have reprogrammed
the phaser banks

00:06:47.773 --> 00:06:49.070
to a rotating modulation,

00:06:49.108 --> 00:06:51.702
but I suspect the Borg
will adapt quickly.

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:53.678
We can use every edge.
Ensign?

00:06:53.712 --> 00:06:55.509
I've already configured
the long-range sensors

00:06:55.548 --> 00:06:57.413
to scan for transwarp
signatures...

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:58.849
an early-warning system.

00:06:58.884 --> 00:07:00.112
Good work.

00:07:00.152 --> 00:07:01.881
Doctor, how are you coming
on the medical front?

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:03.821
I've analyzed
every square millimeter

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:06.381
of the Borg corpse
we recovered three months ago.

00:07:06.425 --> 00:07:07.915
I'm closer to understanding

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:10.155
how their assimilation
technology works

00:07:10.196 --> 00:07:12.790
and I might be able to create
some sort of medical defense.

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:13.924
Redouble your efforts.

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:15.432
This is your top priority.

00:07:15.468 --> 00:07:19.063
Neelix, I doubt we can
resupply the ship any time soon.

00:07:19.104 --> 00:07:20.128
No problem, sir.

00:07:20.172 --> 00:07:21.935
I'm working on a plan
to extend our food

00:07:22.007 --> 00:07:23.338
and replicator rations.

00:07:23.375 --> 00:07:25.070
We have to act fast.

00:07:26.812 --> 00:07:28.871
The Borg have captured
one of our probes.

00:07:28.914 --> 00:07:30.211
They know we're out here.

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:34.709
We'll do everything in our power
to avoid a direct confrontation,

00:07:34.753 --> 00:07:36.846
but, if and when
we do engage the Borg,

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:39.824
I'm confident
that we'll be ready.

00:07:39.859 --> 00:07:43.556
I have faith
in each and every one of you.

00:07:45.164 --> 00:07:46.654
Let's do it.

00:07:57.643 --> 00:07:58.667
Coming through.

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:01.311
Open!

00:08:06.886 --> 00:08:09.548
I want to cut down the time it
takes to seal off the decks.

00:08:09.588 --> 00:08:11.283
In case we take on
some uninvited guests.

00:08:11.323 --> 00:08:12.620
Exactly. And I want

00:08:12.658 --> 00:08:14.785
to increase the magnitude
of the force fields.

00:08:16.495 --> 00:08:18.827
These injection tubules
are the first step

00:08:18.864 --> 00:08:20.661
in the Borg
assimilation process.

00:08:20.699 --> 00:08:21.859
Once inside the skin,

00:08:21.901 --> 00:08:24.062
they release
a series of nanoprobes

00:08:24.103 --> 00:08:25.468
into the bloodstream.

00:08:25.504 --> 00:08:26.937
Maybe we can develop some type

00:08:27.039 --> 00:08:28.939
of protective shielding
against them.

00:08:29.008 --> 00:08:30.339
Unlikely.

00:08:30.376 --> 00:08:32.708
The tubules are capable
of penetrating

00:08:32.745 --> 00:08:34.804
any known alloy
or energy field...

00:08:34.847 --> 00:08:37.338
which means our battle
must be waged

00:08:37.383 --> 00:08:38.748
inside the body itself.

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:42.412
The first tissue

00:08:42.454 --> 00:08:43.785
to be attacked
by the nanoprobes

00:08:43.822 --> 00:08:44.948
is the victim's blood.

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:46.855
Assimilation is
almost instantaneous.

00:08:46.892 --> 00:08:48.883
They take over
the blood cell functions

00:08:48.928 --> 00:08:50.156
like a virus.

00:08:50.195 --> 00:08:52.095
Which suggests to me
that we should try

00:08:52.131 --> 00:08:53.598
to enhance the immune system...

00:08:53.632 --> 00:08:56.226
create an "assimilation
antibody" as it were.

00:08:56.268 --> 00:08:59.635
I doubt we can actually
destroy the nanoprobes,

00:08:59.672 --> 00:09:02.641
but we might be able
to slow them down.

00:09:02.675 --> 00:09:05.007
Let's try a submicron

00:09:05.044 --> 00:09:07.672
dissection on the probes
we've collected so far,

00:09:07.713 --> 00:09:10.147
see if we can discover
the assimilation mechanism.

00:09:17.456 --> 00:09:19.890
Kes, is something wrong?

00:09:21.293 --> 00:09:23.261
Kes.

00:09:23.295 --> 00:09:24.785
I saw Borg.

00:09:27.066 --> 00:09:28.931
You've had
a telepathic experience?

00:09:29.001 --> 00:09:30.628
There were bodies...

00:09:30.669 --> 00:09:32.933
dozens of them dead.

00:09:42.781 --> 00:09:43.941
How's Kes?

00:09:44.016 --> 00:09:46.314
Unsettled and uncertain.

00:09:46.352 --> 00:09:47.819
Over the past two hours,

00:09:47.853 --> 00:09:50.287
she has experienced
several telepathic visions

00:09:50.322 --> 00:09:53.553
about the death of Borg
and the destruction of Voyager.

00:09:53.592 --> 00:09:55.116
Some sort of premonitions?

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:56.354
Possibly.

00:09:56.395 --> 00:09:58.625
We can't just ignore
her intuition,

00:09:58.664 --> 00:10:01.292
but I see no reason
to alter our plan.

00:10:01.333 --> 00:10:02.800
Tuvok, I want you
to keep an eye on her...

00:10:02.835 --> 00:10:03.802
Captain...

00:10:03.836 --> 00:10:05.133
long-range sensors
are picking up

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:06.694
transwarp signatures.

00:10:06.739 --> 00:10:08.468
5.8 light-years distant...

00:10:08.507 --> 00:10:09.974
closing from behind.

00:10:10.042 --> 00:10:11.277
Red Alert.

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:12.900
Evasive maneuvers.

00:10:16.148 --> 00:10:17.877
What's happening?

00:10:17.916 --> 00:10:19.144
We've dropped out of warp.

00:10:19.184 --> 00:10:21.175
Bridge to Engineering.
What's going on down there?

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:22.778
I'm not sure, Captain.

00:10:22.821 --> 00:10:24.789
Some kind of subspace
turbulence is preventing us

00:10:24.823 --> 00:10:26.814
from creating
a stable warp field.

00:10:26.859 --> 00:10:28.520
Turbulence is increasing.

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:30.187
I'm reading two Borg vessels.

00:10:30.229 --> 00:10:31.719
Make that three.

00:10:31.764 --> 00:10:33.732
Four.

00:10:33.766 --> 00:10:35.825
No, five.

00:10:37.603 --> 00:10:39.730
15 Borg vessels.

00:10:39.772 --> 00:10:42.400
Distance:
2.1 light-years and closing.

00:10:42.441 --> 00:10:43.601
Shields to maximum.

00:10:43.642 --> 00:10:44.939
Stand by all weapons.

00:10:44.977 --> 00:10:46.467
They're in visual range.

00:10:46.512 --> 00:10:47.706
On screen.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.411
My god.

00:11:03.896 --> 00:11:04.920
Captain...

00:11:06.565 --> 00:11:09.466
I'm picking up a polaron beam.

00:11:09.501 --> 00:11:11.230
We're being scanned.

00:11:16.108 --> 00:11:17.939
Think good thoughts.

00:11:22.247 --> 00:11:24.408
The last cube
has rejoined the others.

00:11:33.325 --> 00:11:34.758
Did we sustain any damage?

00:11:34.793 --> 00:11:36.454
No. Shields held.

00:11:36.495 --> 00:11:38.520
Warp engines are
coming back on line.

00:11:38.564 --> 00:11:40.555
All primary systems are stable.

00:11:40.599 --> 00:11:41.861
Stand down Red Alert.

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:45.461
Harry... maintain
a long-range sensor lock

00:11:45.504 --> 00:11:47.267
on that Borg armada.

00:11:47.306 --> 00:11:49.240
They seemed to be in quite
a hurry, didn't they?

00:11:49.274 --> 00:11:51.003
I'd like to know
what they're up to.

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:52.304
Yes, ma'am.

00:11:52.344 --> 00:11:54.744
I'll take this near-miss
as a good omen.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:57.248
Resume our course, Mr. Paris.

00:11:57.282 --> 00:12:00.012
If we needed any more evidence
that we've entered Borg space,

00:12:00.119 --> 00:12:01.279
I think we just got it.

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:03.049
I'll be in my ready room.

00:12:18.404 --> 00:12:19.837
Yes. Come in.

00:12:22.441 --> 00:12:24.773
We've just completed
the latest sensor sweep.

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:25.868
So far, so good.

00:12:25.911 --> 00:12:28.573
The Northwest Passage
is still clear of Borg activity.

00:12:28.614 --> 00:12:30.639
I'd like to see
a tactical update.

00:12:32.484 --> 00:12:34.349
According to my calculations,

00:12:34.386 --> 00:12:37.082
neither of us has eaten
since last night.

00:12:37.122 --> 00:12:39.317
Join me for dinner?

00:12:39.358 --> 00:12:40.882
No, thanks.
I'm not hungry.

00:12:40.926 --> 00:12:42.553
I've got a lot of work to do.

00:12:42.594 --> 00:12:44.494
I see.

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:46.760
I've been looking through
the personal log entries

00:12:46.799 --> 00:12:49.996
of all the Starfleet Captains
who encountered the Borg.

00:12:50.102 --> 00:12:51.660
I've gone over every engagement

00:12:51.703 --> 00:12:53.933
from the moment
Q flung the Enterprise

00:12:53.972 --> 00:12:56.202
into the path of that first cube

00:12:56.241 --> 00:13:00.974
to the massacre at Wolf 359...
every battle, every skirmish,

00:13:01.013 --> 00:13:02.310
anything that might
give me an insight

00:13:02.347 --> 00:13:03.507
into the mind of the collective.

00:13:03.549 --> 00:13:04.538
And?

00:13:04.583 --> 00:13:07.950
In the words
of Jean-Luc Picard...

00:13:07.986 --> 00:13:10.784
"In their collective state,

00:13:10.823 --> 00:13:14.589
"the Borg are utterly
without mercy...

00:13:14.626 --> 00:13:16.423
"driven by one will alone...

00:13:16.462 --> 00:13:18.327
"the will to conquer.

00:13:18.363 --> 00:13:22.527
They are beyond redemption,
beyond reason."

00:13:22.568 --> 00:13:25.594
And then there's Captain Amasov
of the Endeavor.

00:13:25.637 --> 00:13:30.904
"It is my opinion that the Borg
are as close to pure evil

00:13:30.943 --> 00:13:33.207
as any race
we've ever encountered..."

00:13:33.245 --> 00:13:34.644
What's so funny?

00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:35.669
Uh, nothing.

00:13:35.714 --> 00:13:36.806
You're smiling.

00:13:36.849 --> 00:13:38.840
Obviously, I've said
something amusing.

00:13:38.884 --> 00:13:41.284
You sounded just like Amasov.

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:42.514
What?

00:13:42.554 --> 00:13:44.181
Just now, while you
were reading his log,

00:13:44.223 --> 00:13:45.918
you were using his inflections.

00:13:45.958 --> 00:13:47.789
- I did not.
- Yes, you were.

00:13:47.826 --> 00:13:49.987
And before that, you were
doing a pretty good Picard.

00:13:50.028 --> 00:13:51.461
Was I?

00:13:51.497 --> 00:13:53.624
It's nothing to be
ashamed about...

00:13:53.665 --> 00:13:55.758
echoing the greats.

00:13:55.801 --> 00:13:58.827
Ensign Hickman in Astrophysics
does a passable Janeway.

00:14:00.839 --> 00:14:02.807
If we manage to survive
the next few days,

00:14:02.841 --> 00:14:04.638
I'm going to have a little
chat with Ensign Hickman.

00:14:04.676 --> 00:14:06.803
Imitating the Captain, huh?

00:14:06.845 --> 00:14:10.303
Surely that violates some kind
of Starfleet protocol.

00:14:15.654 --> 00:14:17.747
This day was inevitable.

00:14:17.789 --> 00:14:20.952
We all knew it
and we've all tried

00:14:20.993 --> 00:14:24.292
to prepare ourselves
for the challenge ahead.

00:14:26.532 --> 00:14:29.399
But at what point is
the risk too great?

00:14:30.936 --> 00:14:32.699
At what point do we come about

00:14:32.738 --> 00:14:34.797
and retreat
to friendly territory?

00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:36.967
Could the crew accept living out

00:14:37.075 --> 00:14:39.475
the rest of their lives
in the Delta Quadrant?

00:14:39.511 --> 00:14:40.978
I keep looking
to all these Captains...

00:14:41.013 --> 00:14:43.379
my comrades in arms.

00:14:43.415 --> 00:14:45.576
But the truth is...

00:14:45.617 --> 00:14:47.380
I'm alone.

00:14:47.419 --> 00:14:49.887
If that moment comes...

00:14:49.922 --> 00:14:51.617
we'll face it together

00:14:51.657 --> 00:14:54.217
and we'll make
the right decision.

00:14:54.259 --> 00:14:56.819
You're not alone, Kathryn.

00:14:59.531 --> 00:15:02.898
Three years ago, I didn't
even know your name.

00:15:02.935 --> 00:15:06.063
Today, I can't imagine
a day without you.

00:15:06.104 --> 00:15:08.038
Captain Janeway to the Bridge.

00:15:14.212 --> 00:15:16.043
Gentlemen?

00:15:16.081 --> 00:15:17.673
Something strange is going on.

00:15:17.716 --> 00:15:19.377
The power signatures
of those Borg vessels

00:15:19.418 --> 00:15:20.385
have terminated.

00:15:20.419 --> 00:15:21.386
All of them?

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:22.682
They're dead in the water...

00:15:22.721 --> 00:15:24.621
about 5.2 light-years
from here.

00:15:24.656 --> 00:15:25.623
Cause.

00:15:25.657 --> 00:15:26.624
Unknown.

00:15:26.658 --> 00:15:29.388
Mr. Paris...

00:15:29.428 --> 00:15:30.656
Captain.

00:15:30.696 --> 00:15:35.497
Set a course
for their position... warp 2.

00:15:39.938 --> 00:15:41.701
We're approaching the ships.

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:43.105
Slow to impulse.

00:15:43.141 --> 00:15:44.438
On screen.

00:15:52.718 --> 00:15:53.776
Life signs.

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:56.985
A few but they're erratic.

00:15:57.055 --> 00:15:58.386
Captain,

00:15:58.423 --> 00:16:01.915
I'm detecting two residual
weapon signatures in the debris.

00:16:02.027 --> 00:16:05.019
One is Borg.

00:16:05.063 --> 00:16:08.294
The other is of unknown origin.

00:16:08.333 --> 00:16:09.925
Who could do this to the Borg?

00:16:20.445 --> 00:16:22.606
Someone more powerful
than the Borg?

00:16:22.648 --> 00:16:23.945
It's hard to imagine.

00:16:23.982 --> 00:16:27.713
But they did it... 15 cubes.

00:16:27.753 --> 00:16:29.721
We might have just
found our ticket

00:16:29.755 --> 00:16:31.382
through Borg space... an ally.

00:16:31.423 --> 00:16:33.618
Let's not jump to conclusions.

00:16:33.659 --> 00:16:36.526
Scan the vicinity
for other vessels.

00:16:37.529 --> 00:16:38.496
There are none.

00:16:38.530 --> 00:16:39.861
Hold on.

00:16:39.898 --> 00:16:42.264
I'm picking up
some sort of bio-readings.

00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:44.598
They're coming from the outer
hull of one of the Borg ships.

00:16:44.636 --> 00:16:45.728
Let's see it.

00:16:48.707 --> 00:16:50.834
Magnify, Mr. Kim.

00:16:52.678 --> 00:16:53.944
It's definitely organic,

00:16:54.077 --> 00:16:56.068
but our sensors can't
penetrate its surface.

00:16:56.112 --> 00:16:57.602
Send a standard greeting.

00:16:58.882 --> 00:16:59.974
No response.

00:17:00.083 --> 00:17:02.074
This could be
a space-dwelling organism

00:17:02.118 --> 00:17:03.346
or a biological weapon.

00:17:03.386 --> 00:17:06.446
I'd like to know what kind of
weapon could destroy the Borg.

00:17:06.489 --> 00:17:08.354
Can we beam it
away from the ship?

00:17:08.391 --> 00:17:10.325
I can't get a lock on it.

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:11.452
Tractor beam?

00:17:12.629 --> 00:17:14.028
No effect.

00:17:14.064 --> 00:17:16.294
Whatever that thing is,

00:17:16.333 --> 00:17:18.392
it's impervious
to our technology.

00:17:18.435 --> 00:17:20.403
Tuvok...

00:17:20.437 --> 00:17:23.770
are you reading an atmosphere
in the cube?

00:17:23.807 --> 00:17:25.274
Affirmative.

00:17:25.308 --> 00:17:26.900
Commander Chakotay.

00:17:29.846 --> 00:17:32.041
I want you to take
an away team inside.

00:17:32.082 --> 00:17:34.949
Try to get a short-range
scan of the bio-mass.

00:17:35.018 --> 00:17:37.851
There are still Borg life signs,
but they're unstable.

00:17:37.887 --> 00:17:40.378
We'll keep an open com-link
and an active transporter lock,

00:17:40.423 --> 00:17:41.651
and we will pull you
out of there

00:17:41.691 --> 00:17:42.817
at the first sign of trouble.

00:17:44.794 --> 00:17:46.318
Tuvok, Harry...

00:17:46.363 --> 00:17:47.523
you're with me.

00:18:19.496 --> 00:18:20.827
This way.

00:18:36.513 --> 00:18:38.344
Lower your phasers.

00:18:38.381 --> 00:18:40.906
If we don't appear threatening,
they should ignore us.

00:18:40.950 --> 00:18:43.885
Looks like they're
a little preoccupied.

00:19:14.851 --> 00:19:17.251
The alien bio-readings
are getting stronger.

00:19:17.287 --> 00:19:18.652
We're close.

00:19:30.333 --> 00:19:31.766
Commander?

00:19:38.041 --> 00:19:39.030
Curious.

00:19:39.075 --> 00:19:41.168
That's not the word
I had in mind.

00:19:41.211 --> 00:19:42.644
Those bodies are reminiscent

00:19:42.679 --> 00:19:44.874
of one of the premonitions
Kes described.

00:19:44.914 --> 00:19:47.849
Didn't Kes say we were
all going to die?

00:19:50.286 --> 00:19:51.753
Let's keep moving.

00:20:23.786 --> 00:20:25.413
It looks like the bio-mass

00:20:25.455 --> 00:20:27.184
dissolved right
through the Borg hull.

00:20:27.223 --> 00:20:30.886
This Borg is attempting
to assimilate it.

00:20:30.927 --> 00:20:33.657
Doesn't look like he's
having much luck.

00:20:38.568 --> 00:20:40.900
There's a chamber
beyond this opening...

00:20:40.937 --> 00:20:42.097
40 meters wide,

00:20:42.138 --> 00:20:44.368
high concentrations
of antimatter particles.

00:20:44.407 --> 00:20:47.740
It looks like a warp propulsion
system of some kind.

00:20:47.777 --> 00:20:49.176
It's a ship?

00:20:49.212 --> 00:20:50.907
Starfleet has encountered
species

00:20:50.947 --> 00:20:52.812
that use
organic-based vessels...

00:20:52.849 --> 00:20:53.907
the Breen for example.

00:20:53.950 --> 00:20:56.214
There doesn't seem
to be anybody inside.

00:20:56.252 --> 00:20:58.846
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:20:58.888 --> 00:21:00.879
Go ahead, Commander.

00:21:00.924 --> 00:21:04.291
Captain, we've found
an entrance to the bio-mass.

00:21:04.327 --> 00:21:06.420
We think it might be
a ship of some kind.

00:21:06.462 --> 00:21:07.952
Permission to go inside.

00:21:07.997 --> 00:21:09.157
Granted.

00:21:09.199 --> 00:21:12.691
Harry, that's a Borg
distribution node.

00:21:12.735 --> 00:21:15.203
See if you can download
their tactical database.

00:21:15.238 --> 00:21:17.069
It might contain a record
of what happened here.

00:21:17.106 --> 00:21:18.164
Aye, sir.

00:21:18.208 --> 00:21:19.300
Tuvok.

00:21:53.376 --> 00:21:55.367
They seem to be
organic conduits.

00:21:55.411 --> 00:21:57.276
They're carrying
electrodynamic fluid.

00:21:57.313 --> 00:21:59.008
It may be an energy source.

00:21:59.048 --> 00:22:00.447
Maybe.

00:22:02.619 --> 00:22:05.053
This looks like a binary matrix,

00:22:05.088 --> 00:22:07.215
but it's laced
with neuropeptides.

00:22:07.257 --> 00:22:09.418
Could be their version
of a computer core.

00:22:47.930 --> 00:22:50.831
This damage was caused
by a Borg disruptor beam.

00:22:50.867 --> 00:22:52.858
The wall appears
to be regenerating itself.

00:23:03.413 --> 00:23:05.608
Commander.

00:23:34.043 --> 00:23:35.237
Kes?

00:23:35.278 --> 00:23:36.245
Harry's in danger.

00:23:36.279 --> 00:23:37.246
What do you see?

00:23:37.280 --> 00:23:38.247
Get them out of there!

00:23:38.281 --> 00:23:39.270
Sick Bay to Janeway.

00:23:39.315 --> 00:23:40.680
Commander!

00:23:45.822 --> 00:23:47.255
There's something
in here with us

00:23:47.290 --> 00:23:48.882
and it's not the Borg.

00:23:48.925 --> 00:23:51.689
I can't localize it,
but it's within 20 meters.

00:23:51.728 --> 00:23:53.252
Perhaps the pilot has returned.

00:23:53.296 --> 00:23:55.457
Voyager to away team.

00:23:55.498 --> 00:23:56.522
Go ahead.

00:23:56.566 --> 00:23:58.534
Stand by for transport.

00:23:58.568 --> 00:23:59.660
We're getting you out of there.

00:23:59.702 --> 00:24:00.669
Good idea.

00:24:00.703 --> 00:24:01.670
Energize.

00:24:02.805 --> 00:24:04.170
I can't get a lock on them.

00:24:04.207 --> 00:24:05.538
What's the problem?

00:24:05.575 --> 00:24:06.940
It looks like
bio-electric interference

00:24:07.009 --> 00:24:08.340
from whatever's
coming toward them.

00:24:09.645 --> 00:24:11.579
It's within seven meters.

00:24:11.614 --> 00:24:13.411
Let's get out of here.

00:24:15.752 --> 00:24:17.515
Narrow the confinement beam.

00:24:17.553 --> 00:24:19.544
No effect.

00:24:19.589 --> 00:24:22.057
I'm going to try
a skeletal lock.

00:24:22.091 --> 00:24:23.217
A what?

00:24:23.259 --> 00:24:24.726
I think I can get a clean lock

00:24:24.761 --> 00:24:26.592
on the minerals
in their bone tissue.

00:24:26.629 --> 00:24:29.223
I just came up with it,
but I think it might work.

00:24:43.346 --> 00:24:45.814
The life-form's five meters away
and closing.

00:24:45.848 --> 00:24:47.145
From where?

00:24:59.594 --> 00:25:01.425
I've got them.

00:25:01.463 --> 00:25:03.328
A skeletal lock, huh?

00:25:03.365 --> 00:25:05.731
We'll have to add that one
to the transporter manual.

00:25:06.768 --> 00:25:08.099
Captain.

00:25:08.136 --> 00:25:11.071
The bioship is powering up...
like it's charging

00:25:11.106 --> 00:25:12.471
some kind of weapon.

00:25:15.043 --> 00:25:18.672
Mr. Paris, get us out of here...
maximum warp.

00:25:45.540 --> 00:25:47.838
The alien ship is not pursuing.

00:25:51.212 --> 00:25:53.112
Kes?

00:25:53.148 --> 00:25:54.945
I could hear its thoughts.

00:25:54.983 --> 00:25:56.473
The pilot of the bioship

00:25:56.518 --> 00:25:58.247
was trying
to communicate with me.

00:26:00.088 --> 00:26:02.079
They're a telepathic species.

00:26:02.123 --> 00:26:04.489
I've been aware of them
for some time now...

00:26:04.526 --> 00:26:05.823
the premonitions.

00:26:05.860 --> 00:26:08.192
Captain, it's not the Borg
that we should be worried about.

00:26:08.229 --> 00:26:09.196
It's them.

00:26:09.230 --> 00:26:11.323
What did it say to you?

00:26:11.366 --> 00:26:13.425
It said...

00:26:16.004 --> 00:26:18.063
"The weak...

00:26:18.106 --> 00:26:19.835
will perish."

00:26:28.149 --> 00:26:31.846
Captain's Log, Stardate 50984.3.

00:26:31.886 --> 00:26:33.285
It's been 12 hours

00:26:33.321 --> 00:26:35.721
since our confrontation
with the alien life-form.

00:26:35.757 --> 00:26:38.749
There's no sign
that we're being pursued

00:26:38.793 --> 00:26:41.785
and we've had no further
encounters with the Borg.

00:26:41.830 --> 00:26:44.094
I've decided to hold our course.

00:26:44.132 --> 00:26:46.692
The Northwest Passage
is only one day away

00:26:46.735 --> 00:26:48.134
and I won't allow fear

00:26:48.169 --> 00:26:50.831
to undermine
this crew's sense of purpose...

00:26:50.872 --> 00:26:53.340
even if that fear is justified.

00:26:59.247 --> 00:27:00.942
The infection is spreading.

00:27:00.982 --> 00:27:03.143
What began
with a few stray cells

00:27:03.184 --> 00:27:04.879
contaminating the chest wound

00:27:04.919 --> 00:27:07.353
is now infusing
every system in his body.

00:27:07.389 --> 00:27:10.449
It looks like he's being
transformed in some way.

00:27:10.492 --> 00:27:12.016
Not exactly.

00:27:12.060 --> 00:27:14.528
The alien cells are
consuming his body

00:27:14.562 --> 00:27:15.927
from the inside out.

00:27:15.964 --> 00:27:17.625
In essence...

00:27:17.665 --> 00:27:20.657
Mr. Kim is being eaten alive.

00:27:20.702 --> 00:27:23.034
He's still conscious, Doctor?

00:27:23.071 --> 00:27:25.938
I tried giving him a sedative,
but it was rejected immediately.

00:27:26.041 --> 00:27:27.702
In fact,
every treatment I've tried

00:27:27.742 --> 00:27:29.801
has been neutralized
within seconds.

00:27:35.050 --> 00:27:37.814
These are alien cells.

00:27:37.852 --> 00:27:39.717
Each one contains

00:27:39.754 --> 00:27:42.723
more than a hundred times
the DNA of a human cell.

00:27:42.757 --> 00:27:45.954
It's the most densely coded
life-form I've ever seen.

00:27:46.061 --> 00:27:48.393
Even I would need years
to decipher it.

00:27:48.430 --> 00:27:51.957
They have an extraordinary
immune response.

00:27:52.067 --> 00:27:55.559
Anything that penetrates
the cell membrane...

00:27:55.603 --> 00:27:57.798
chemical... biological...

00:27:57.839 --> 00:27:59.568
technological...

00:28:01.409 --> 00:28:03.900
it's all instantly destroyed.

00:28:04.012 --> 00:28:06.480
That's why the Borg
can't assimilate them.

00:28:06.514 --> 00:28:10.245
Resistance in this case
is far from futile.

00:28:10.285 --> 00:28:13.584
Nevertheless,
I believe Borg technology

00:28:13.621 --> 00:28:15.782
holds the key to saving Mr. Kim.

00:28:15.824 --> 00:28:17.086
How so?

00:28:17.125 --> 00:28:19.616
I hope to unleash
an army of modified

00:28:19.661 --> 00:28:21.720
Borg nanoprobes
into his bloodstream

00:28:21.763 --> 00:28:24.391
designed to target
and eradicate the infection.

00:28:24.432 --> 00:28:27.799
As you know, I've been
analyzing the nanoprobes.

00:28:27.836 --> 00:28:30.532
They're efficient
little assimilators.

00:28:30.572 --> 00:28:32.597
One can't help
but admire the workmanship.

00:28:32.640 --> 00:28:34.938
But they're no match
for the alien cells.

00:28:35.043 --> 00:28:39.810
So I successfully
dissected a nanoprobe

00:28:39.848 --> 00:28:43.215
and managed to access
its recoding mechanism.

00:28:43.251 --> 00:28:44.411
I reprogrammed the probe

00:28:44.452 --> 00:28:46.579
to emit the same
electrochemical signatures

00:28:46.621 --> 00:28:48.213
as the alien cells.

00:28:48.256 --> 00:28:50.315
That way, the probe
can do its work

00:28:50.358 --> 00:28:52.087
without being detected.

00:28:52.127 --> 00:28:53.219
Observe.

00:28:53.261 --> 00:28:56.788
The alien cells are completely
oblivious to the probe

00:28:56.831 --> 00:28:58.458
until it's too late.

00:28:58.500 --> 00:29:01.594
Unfortunately, I've only
created a few prototypes.

00:29:02.937 --> 00:29:04.199
I'll need several days

00:29:04.239 --> 00:29:07.470
to modify enough nanoprobes
to cure Ensign Kim.

00:29:07.509 --> 00:29:09.875
Does Harry have several days?

00:29:09.911 --> 00:29:11.708
I wish I knew.

00:29:20.755 --> 00:29:23.155
Fight it, Harry.

00:29:23.191 --> 00:29:25.682
That's an order.

00:29:29.063 --> 00:29:31.531
We've analyzed the Borg's
tactical database.

00:29:31.566 --> 00:29:32.794
They refer to these new aliens

00:29:32.834 --> 00:29:35.667
as "Species 8472."

00:29:35.703 --> 00:29:36.931
Over the past five months,

00:29:36.971 --> 00:29:38.199
the Borg have been
attacked by them

00:29:38.239 --> 00:29:39.831
on at least a dozen occasions.

00:29:39.874 --> 00:29:41.603
Each time, the Borg
were defeated swiftly.

00:29:41.643 --> 00:29:43.338
The collective has
very little information

00:29:43.378 --> 00:29:44.675
about the species.

00:29:44.712 --> 00:29:46.646
Is anything known
about where they come from?

00:29:48.016 --> 00:29:49.813
I'm afraid so.

00:29:53.321 --> 00:29:55.084
Get the Captain.

00:29:57.358 --> 00:30:00.088
The Northwest Passage.

00:30:00.128 --> 00:30:03.620
It's clear of Borg activity
for a very good reason.

00:30:03.665 --> 00:30:05.565
I'm detecting 133 bioships.

00:30:05.600 --> 00:30:06.897
More are approaching.

00:30:06.935 --> 00:30:08.493
From where?

00:30:08.536 --> 00:30:11.266
They seem to be coming
from a quantum singularity.

00:30:11.306 --> 00:30:13.365
I'm localizing
the gravimetric distortions.

00:30:13.408 --> 00:30:15.069
On screen.

00:30:20.081 --> 00:30:21.605
Kes?

00:30:21.649 --> 00:30:22.980
Anything?

00:30:23.051 --> 00:30:24.382
Yes, I can hear them.

00:30:29.324 --> 00:30:31.121
They're in a place
where they're all alone.

00:30:31.159 --> 00:30:32.251
Nothing else lives there.

00:30:32.293 --> 00:30:34.352
Some kind of parallel universe?

00:30:34.395 --> 00:30:35.657
I don't know.

00:30:37.198 --> 00:30:38.859
I feel malevolence...

00:30:38.900 --> 00:30:40.993
a cold hatred.

00:30:41.102 --> 00:30:43.696
The weak will perish.

00:30:45.373 --> 00:30:47.000
It's an invasion.

00:30:47.075 --> 00:30:49.976
They intend
on destroying everything.

00:30:50.011 --> 00:30:52.172
Tom, reverse course,
maximum warp.

00:30:52.213 --> 00:30:54.306
Take us five light-years out
and hold position.

00:30:54.349 --> 00:30:55.316
Aye, Captain.

00:30:55.350 --> 00:30:56.578
Maintain Red Alert.

00:30:56.618 --> 00:30:58.677
Commander?

00:31:07.862 --> 00:31:09.955
That moment we spoke about?
It's here.

00:31:09.998 --> 00:31:11.465
Any thoughts?

00:31:11.499 --> 00:31:12.864
Just one.

00:31:12.900 --> 00:31:14.629
Flying into that corridor
would mean certain death.

00:31:14.669 --> 00:31:15.863
Agreed.

00:31:15.903 --> 00:31:17.928
The Northwest Passage
is no longer an option.

00:31:17.972 --> 00:31:22.204
So now the choice is between
facing the Borg in their space

00:31:22.243 --> 00:31:24.973
or finding a nice planet
here in the Delta Quadrant

00:31:25.046 --> 00:31:27.742
and giving up
on ever getting home.

00:31:27.782 --> 00:31:30.080
We'd be turning around,
but we wouldn't be giving up.

00:31:30.118 --> 00:31:32.814
We may find another way home.

00:31:35.156 --> 00:31:36.748
I'm not ready to walk
onto that Bridge

00:31:36.791 --> 00:31:38.224
and tell the crew
we're quitting.

00:31:38.259 --> 00:31:39.886
I can't do it, Chakotay,
not yet.

00:31:39.927 --> 00:31:41.986
There must be
another alternative.

00:31:42.096 --> 00:31:46.465
Kathryn, you haven't
slept in two days.

00:31:46.501 --> 00:31:49.561
Try getting some rest
and clearing your head.

00:31:49.604 --> 00:31:51.469
We're safe for the moment.

00:31:51.506 --> 00:31:54.031
We can tell the crew
tomorrow if we have to.

00:31:55.043 --> 00:31:56.840
See you in the morning.

00:32:24.939 --> 00:32:26.634
Maestro?

00:32:31.245 --> 00:32:32.439
Leonardo.

00:32:36.384 --> 00:32:37.976
Catarina...

00:32:38.052 --> 00:32:39.246
buona sera.

00:32:39.287 --> 00:32:40.914
Am I disturbing you?

00:32:40.955 --> 00:32:43.150
What do you see?

00:32:44.959 --> 00:32:46.358
A wall

00:32:46.394 --> 00:32:48.487
with candlelight
reflecting on it.

00:32:48.529 --> 00:32:49.996
Why?

00:32:50.098 --> 00:32:52.464
What do you see?

00:32:52.500 --> 00:32:55.669
A flock of starlings...

00:32:55.802 --> 00:32:57.929
the leaves on an oak...

00:32:57.971 --> 00:32:59.370
a horse's tail...

00:32:59.406 --> 00:33:02.500
a thief with a noose
around his neck...

00:33:04.177 --> 00:33:06.111
Ah...

00:33:06.146 --> 00:33:08.410
and a wall...

00:33:08.448 --> 00:33:10.916
with the candlelight
reflecting on it.

00:33:13.987 --> 00:33:15.955
There are times, Catarina,

00:33:16.056 --> 00:33:21.153
when I find myself transfixed
by a shadow on the wall

00:33:21.194 --> 00:33:24.220
or the splashing of water
against a stone.

00:33:24.264 --> 00:33:27.961
I stare at it, the hours pass...

00:33:28.034 --> 00:33:31.800
the world around me
drops away...

00:33:31.838 --> 00:33:37.071
replaced by worlds
being created and destroyed

00:33:37.110 --> 00:33:40.568
by my imagination...

00:33:42.082 --> 00:33:45.449
a way to focus the mind.

00:33:45.485 --> 00:33:49.285
Sit and tell me
why you have come.

00:33:57.597 --> 00:33:59.531
There's a path before me...

00:33:59.566 --> 00:34:02.330
the only way home.

00:34:02.368 --> 00:34:04.836
And on either side,

00:34:04.871 --> 00:34:08.170
mortal enemies
bent on destroying each other.

00:34:08.208 --> 00:34:10.938
If I attempt
to pass through them,

00:34:10.977 --> 00:34:13.468
I'll be destroyed as well.

00:34:13.513 --> 00:34:15.174
But if I turn around,

00:34:15.215 --> 00:34:19.914
that would end all hope
of ever getting home.

00:34:19.953 --> 00:34:23.650
And no matter how much
I try to focus my mind,

00:34:23.690 --> 00:34:26.284
I can't see an alternative.

00:34:26.326 --> 00:34:33.232
When one's imagination
cannot provide an answer,

00:34:33.266 --> 00:34:37.134
one must seek out
a greater imagination.

00:34:37.170 --> 00:34:41.163
There are times
when even I find myself

00:34:41.207 --> 00:34:43.368
kneeling in prayer.

00:34:43.409 --> 00:34:48.346
I must deliver a bronzetto
to the monks at Santa Croce.

00:34:48.381 --> 00:34:52.818
Come with me, Catarina, eh?

00:34:52.852 --> 00:34:55.980
We will awake the abbot,
visit the chapel

00:34:56.055 --> 00:34:58.114
and appeal to God.

00:34:58.158 --> 00:35:01.525
Somehow I don't think
that's going to work for me.

00:35:10.637 --> 00:35:14.073
But there is an alternative
I hadn't considered.

00:35:16.709 --> 00:35:19.803
What if I made an appeal...

00:35:21.347 --> 00:35:23.076
to the devil?

00:35:27.487 --> 00:35:29.387
An alliance with the Borg?

00:35:29.422 --> 00:35:32.289
More like... an exchange.

00:35:32.325 --> 00:35:35.658
We offer them a way
to defeat their new enemy

00:35:35.695 --> 00:35:40.394
and, in return, we get safe
passage through their space.

00:35:40.433 --> 00:35:41.798
In developing
a treatment for Harry,

00:35:41.835 --> 00:35:43.962
the Doctor has found a way
to attack the aliens

00:35:44.037 --> 00:35:45.664
at a microscopic level.

00:35:45.705 --> 00:35:47.798
It's still in the experimental
stages, Captain.

00:35:47.841 --> 00:35:49.468
I've only made a few prototypes.

00:35:49.509 --> 00:35:50.976
Nevertheless,
if we teach the Borg

00:35:51.044 --> 00:35:52.636
how to modify
their own nanoprobes,

00:35:52.679 --> 00:35:53.976
they'd have a blueprint

00:35:54.047 --> 00:35:56.311
to create a weapon
to fight the aliens.

00:35:56.349 --> 00:35:58.317
In theory, yes.

00:35:58.351 --> 00:36:01.184
B'Elanna, it's clear
from the Borg database

00:36:01.221 --> 00:36:04.850
that they know practically
nothing about Species 8472.

00:36:04.891 --> 00:36:05.858
That's right.

00:36:05.892 --> 00:36:07.519
The Borg gain knowledge
through assimilation.

00:36:07.560 --> 00:36:09.323
What they can't assimilate,
they can't understand.

00:36:09.362 --> 00:36:10.920
But we don't assimilate.

00:36:11.030 --> 00:36:15.228
We investigate... and in this
case, that's given us an edge.

00:36:15.268 --> 00:36:18.396
We've discovered something
they need.

00:36:18.438 --> 00:36:21.930
But the Borg aren't exactly
known for their diplomacy.

00:36:22.008 --> 00:36:24.602
How can we expect them
to cooperate with us?

00:36:24.644 --> 00:36:25.906
Normally, the answer
would be no,

00:36:25.945 --> 00:36:27.879
but if what I've learned
from the aliens is true,

00:36:27.914 --> 00:36:30.109
the Borg are losing
this conflict.

00:36:30.149 --> 00:36:31.707
In one regard,
the Borg are no different

00:36:31.751 --> 00:36:35.278
than we are...
they're trying to survive.

00:36:35.321 --> 00:36:37.812
I don't believe they're
going to refuse an offer

00:36:37.857 --> 00:36:39.324
that will help them do that.

00:36:39.359 --> 00:36:40.519
What makes you think the Borg

00:36:40.560 --> 00:36:42.721
won't attempt to take
the information

00:36:42.762 --> 00:36:44.662
by assimilating Voyager
and its crew?

00:36:44.697 --> 00:36:46.688
Because that won't
get them anywhere.

00:36:46.733 --> 00:36:49.725
Doctor, you're
the only one on board

00:36:49.769 --> 00:36:52.067
with full knowledge
of the nanoprobe modifications.

00:36:52.105 --> 00:36:54.198
I want you to transfer
all of that research

00:36:54.240 --> 00:36:55.366
into your holo-matrix.

00:36:55.408 --> 00:36:56.375
Certainly.

00:36:56.409 --> 00:36:58.502
You're my guarantee.

00:36:58.544 --> 00:37:00.876
If the Borg threaten
us in any way,

00:37:00.914 --> 00:37:03.041
we'll simply erase your program.

00:37:03.082 --> 00:37:04.845
But it won't come to that,
Doctor.

00:37:04.884 --> 00:37:08.081
It's in the collective's
own interest to cooperate.

00:37:08.121 --> 00:37:11.557
Voyager is only one ship.

00:37:11.591 --> 00:37:14.151
Our safe passage
is a small price to pay

00:37:14.193 --> 00:37:16.491
for what we're offering
in exchange.

00:37:18.631 --> 00:37:20.724
B'Elanna, assist the Doctor
with his transfer.

00:37:20.767 --> 00:37:21.734
Aye, Captain.

00:37:21.768 --> 00:37:22.928
Mr. Paris...

00:37:23.036 --> 00:37:25.766
locate the nearest Borg vessel

00:37:25.805 --> 00:37:27.705
and lay in a course.

00:37:27.740 --> 00:37:29.367
They shouldn't
be difficult to find.

00:37:29.409 --> 00:37:31.070
Yes, ma'am.

00:37:32.378 --> 00:37:33.868
Dismissed.

00:37:40.453 --> 00:37:42.785
You were awfully quiet.

00:37:43.990 --> 00:37:46.185
I didn't want the others
to hear this,

00:37:46.225 --> 00:37:48.750
but I think what you're
proposing is too great a risk.

00:37:48.795 --> 00:37:50.092
How so?

00:37:51.230 --> 00:37:54.199
There's a story I heard
as a child, a parable,

00:37:54.233 --> 00:37:56.258
and I never forgot it.

00:37:56.302 --> 00:37:59.738
A scorpion was walking along
the bank of a river

00:37:59.772 --> 00:38:02.366
wondering how to get
to the other side.

00:38:02.408 --> 00:38:05.036
Suddenly, he saw a fox.

00:38:05.078 --> 00:38:09.037
He asked the fox to take him
on his back across the river.

00:38:09.082 --> 00:38:13.883
The fox said, "No, if I
do that, you'll sting me

00:38:13.920 --> 00:38:17.219
and I'll drown."

00:38:17.256 --> 00:38:19.224
The scorpion assured him,

00:38:19.258 --> 00:38:22.386
"If I did that,
we'd both drown."

00:38:22.428 --> 00:38:26.626
So the fox thought about
it and finally agreed.

00:38:26.666 --> 00:38:29.863
So the scorpion climbed
up on his back

00:38:29.902 --> 00:38:32.132
and the fox began to swim.

00:38:32.171 --> 00:38:34.662
But halfway across the river,

00:38:34.707 --> 00:38:37.904
the scorpion stung him.

00:38:37.944 --> 00:38:39.935
As the poison filled his veins,

00:38:39.979 --> 00:38:43.437
the fox turned to the scorpion
and said, "Why did you do that?

00:38:43.483 --> 00:38:45.951
Now, you'll drown, too."

00:38:46.052 --> 00:38:48.714
"I couldn't help it,"
said the scorpion.

00:38:48.755 --> 00:38:51.315
"It's my nature."

00:38:53.493 --> 00:38:56.860
I understand the risk

00:38:56.896 --> 00:38:58.158
and I'm not proposing

00:38:58.197 --> 00:39:01.030
that we try to change
the nature of the beast,

00:39:01.067 --> 00:39:02.898
but this is a unique situation.

00:39:02.935 --> 00:39:05.802
To our knowledge, the Borg
have never been so threatened.

00:39:05.838 --> 00:39:07.169
They're vulnerable.

00:39:07.206 --> 00:39:08.867
I think we can take
advantage of that.

00:39:08.908 --> 00:39:11.399
Even if we do somehow
negotiate an exchange,

00:39:11.444 --> 00:39:13.537
how long will they keep up
their end of the bargain?

00:39:13.579 --> 00:39:16.139
It could take months to
get across Borg territory.

00:39:16.182 --> 00:39:18.776
We'd be facing
thousands of systems,

00:39:18.818 --> 00:39:20.285
millions of vessels.

00:39:20.319 --> 00:39:22.287
But only one collective

00:39:22.321 --> 00:39:23.618
and we've got them
over a barrel.

00:39:23.656 --> 00:39:25.920
We don't need to give them
a single bit of information...

00:39:26.025 --> 00:39:27.424
not until we're safe.

00:39:27.460 --> 00:39:28.688
We just need the courage

00:39:28.728 --> 00:39:30.286
to see this through
to the end.

00:39:30.329 --> 00:39:31.921
There are other kinds
of courage...

00:39:31.964 --> 00:39:33.192
like the courage to accept

00:39:33.232 --> 00:39:35.496
that there are some situations
beyond your control.

00:39:35.535 --> 00:39:39.266
Not every problem has
an immediate solution.

00:39:39.305 --> 00:39:40.533
You're suggesting
we turn around.

00:39:40.573 --> 00:39:42.871
Yes. We should get
out of harm's way.

00:39:42.909 --> 00:39:44.342
Let them fight it out.

00:39:44.377 --> 00:39:45.901
In the meantime,
there's still plenty

00:39:45.945 --> 00:39:47.810
of Delta Quadrant
left to explore.

00:39:47.847 --> 00:39:49.815
We may find another way home.

00:39:49.849 --> 00:39:50.941
Or we might find something else.

00:39:51.017 --> 00:39:52.848
Six months,
a year down the road,

00:39:52.885 --> 00:39:55.718
after Species 8472
gets through with the Borg,

00:39:55.755 --> 00:39:57.814
we could find ourselves
right back in the line of fire.

00:39:57.857 --> 00:39:59.415
And we'll have missed
the window of opportunity

00:39:59.459 --> 00:40:01.927
that exists right here,
right now.

00:40:01.961 --> 00:40:03.952
How much is our safety worth?

00:40:04.030 --> 00:40:05.361
What do you mean?

00:40:05.398 --> 00:40:06.865
We'd be giving an advantage

00:40:06.899 --> 00:40:09.094
to a race guilty
of murdering billions.

00:40:09.135 --> 00:40:12.366
We'd be helping the Borg
assimilate yet another species

00:40:12.405 --> 00:40:14.703
just to get ourselves
back home... it's wrong!

00:40:14.740 --> 00:40:15.968
Tell that to Harry Kim.

00:40:16.008 --> 00:40:18.476
He's barely alive
thanks to that species.

00:40:18.511 --> 00:40:21.275
Maybe helping to assimilate them
isn't such a bad idea.

00:40:21.314 --> 00:40:23.214
We could be doing
the Delta Quadrant a favor.

00:40:23.249 --> 00:40:25.774
I don't think
you really believe that.

00:40:25.818 --> 00:40:28.252
I think you're struggling
to justify your plan

00:40:28.287 --> 00:40:30.255
because your desire
to get this crew home

00:40:30.289 --> 00:40:32.189
is blinding you
to other options.

00:40:32.225 --> 00:40:34.090
I know you, Kathryn.

00:40:34.127 --> 00:40:36.561
Sometimes...

00:40:38.131 --> 00:40:40.031
you don't know
when to step back.

00:40:41.067 --> 00:40:42.967
Do you trust me, Chakotay?

00:40:43.002 --> 00:40:43.866
That isn't the issue.

00:40:43.903 --> 00:40:45.200
Oh, but it is.

00:40:45.238 --> 00:40:48.002
Only yesterday, you were saying
that we'd face this together,

00:40:48.040 --> 00:40:49.302
that you'd be at my side.

00:40:49.342 --> 00:40:51.139
I still have to tell you
what I believe.

00:40:51.177 --> 00:40:52.944
I'm no good to you
if I don't do that.

00:40:53.077 --> 00:40:56.171
I appreciate your insights,
but the time for debate is over.

00:40:56.213 --> 00:40:57.942
I've made my decision.

00:40:57.982 --> 00:41:01.543
Now, do I have your support?

00:41:02.720 --> 00:41:04.278
You're the Captain.

00:41:04.322 --> 00:41:05.846
I'm the First Officer.

00:41:05.890 --> 00:41:07.585
I'll follow your orders,

00:41:07.625 --> 00:41:09.616
but that doesn't
change my belief

00:41:09.660 --> 00:41:11.753
that we're making
a fatal mistake.

00:41:13.664 --> 00:41:16.724
Then I guess I am alone
after all.

00:41:19.003 --> 00:41:20.800
Dismissed.

00:41:35.453 --> 00:41:37.353
There are three planets
in this system.

00:41:37.388 --> 00:41:39.652
Inhabitants... all Borg.

00:41:39.690 --> 00:41:41.248
A vessel is approaching.

00:41:41.292 --> 00:41:42.316
All stop.

00:41:42.360 --> 00:41:43.452
Shields up.

00:41:49.500 --> 00:41:50.865
They are hailing us.

00:41:50.901 --> 00:41:52.994
Open a channel.

00:41:53.070 --> 00:41:54.662
We are the Borg.

00:41:54.705 --> 00:41:56.730
You will be assimilated.

00:41:56.774 --> 00:41:58.708
Resistance is futile.

00:42:00.044 --> 00:42:01.875
They've locked on to us
with a tractor beam.

00:42:01.912 --> 00:42:03.573
Borg vessel.

00:42:03.614 --> 00:42:07.072
This is Captain Janeway
of the Starship Voyager.

00:42:07.118 --> 00:42:12.146
I have tactical information
about Species 8472.

00:42:12.189 --> 00:42:14.180
I want to negotiate.

00:42:14.225 --> 00:42:16.193
Negotiation is irrelevant.

00:42:16.227 --> 00:42:17.888
You will be assimilated.

00:42:22.566 --> 00:42:24.796
Borg vessel, what you're

00:42:24.835 --> 00:42:27.827
receiving is a sample
of the knowledge we possess.

00:42:27.872 --> 00:42:30.636
If you don't disengage
your tractor beam immediately,

00:42:30.674 --> 00:42:32.972
I will have that data destroyed.

00:42:33.077 --> 00:42:36.672
You have ten seconds to comply.

00:42:40.284 --> 00:42:42.582
We know you're in danger
of being defeated.

00:42:42.620 --> 00:42:46.215
You can't afford to risk
losing this information.

00:42:46.257 --> 00:42:47.918
Disengage your trac...

00:42:51.729 --> 00:42:53.526
State your demands.

00:42:56.133 --> 00:42:59.193
I want safe passage
through your space.

00:42:59.236 --> 00:43:01.898
Once my ship
is beyond Borg territory,

00:43:01.939 --> 00:43:04.032
I'll give you our research.

00:43:04.075 --> 00:43:06.100
Unacceptable.

00:43:06.143 --> 00:43:09.135
Our space is vast.

00:43:09.180 --> 00:43:12.445
Your passage would
require too much time.

00:43:12.483 --> 00:43:14.781
We need the technology now.

00:43:16.420 --> 00:43:18.354
If I give it to you now,

00:43:18.389 --> 00:43:20.584
you'll assimilate us.

00:43:20.624 --> 00:43:23.957
Species 8472 must be stopped.

00:43:24.061 --> 00:43:27.497
Our survival is your survival.

00:43:27.531 --> 00:43:30.398
Give us the technology.

00:43:32.770 --> 00:43:34.362
No.

00:43:34.405 --> 00:43:37.499
Safe passage first

00:43:37.541 --> 00:43:38.940
or no deal.

00:43:41.779 --> 00:43:44.247
State your proposal.

00:43:44.281 --> 00:43:45.771
Let's work together.

00:43:45.816 --> 00:43:47.909
Combine our resources.

00:43:47.952 --> 00:43:50.682
Even if we do give you
the technology now,

00:43:50.721 --> 00:43:53.519
you're still going to need
time to develop it.

00:43:53.557 --> 00:43:56.151
By working together,

00:43:56.193 --> 00:44:00.095
we can create
a weapon more quickly.

00:44:00.131 --> 00:44:02.326
If you escort us
through your space,

00:44:02.366 --> 00:44:04.334
we can perfect the weapon
as we...

00:44:09.974 --> 00:44:11.874
Where did that ship come from?

00:44:11.909 --> 00:44:14.935
A quantum singularity has
appeared 20,000 kilometers away.

00:44:14.979 --> 00:44:16.776
The bioship is heading
directly toward the planet.

00:44:16.814 --> 00:44:18.281
The Borg shields are weakening.

00:44:18.315 --> 00:44:20.078
We might be able to break
free of the tractor beam.

00:44:20.117 --> 00:44:21.607
Can you get a lock
on the Captain?

00:44:21.652 --> 00:44:23.950
Not yet.

00:44:24.054 --> 00:44:25.578
Commander, there are
nine more bioships

00:44:25.623 --> 00:44:26.954
coming out of the singularity.

00:44:49.346 --> 00:44:51.280
What's going on?
